It's hard to pick out what to disagree with first, but the following stands out as a particularly grievous theological error;

"The Church needs to know and believe that Jesus lives within her and gives her life in the Eucharist, the scriptures and the sacraments."

Jesus lives and gives life within His church through the renewing presence of the Holy Spirit within each and every born again believer. This is confirmed is so many places in the New Testament that I could probably write a book on it, but here's just one quote;

"Do you not know that your bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit, who is in you, whom you have received from God?"

